#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kwordquiz; is a tool that gives you a powerful way to master new "
"vocabularies. It may be a language or any other kind of terminology."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "Easy to use"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With &kwordquiz; you build your own vocabulary documents in a simple and "
"intuitive way. The basic layout is a two-column spreadsheet where you type "
"vocabulary entries in one form that you know and in another form that you "
"want to learn. You change the titles of the columns to reflect what you are "
"practicing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Practice modes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before you start a quiz you select how you want to practice. &kwordquiz; "
"offers five different modes to make practicing more efficient. The different "
"modes make it possible to have the quiz go through your vocabulary in "
"sequential or random order in one or both directions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quiz types"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you have entered your vocabulary and selected a mode you are ready to "
"start a quiz. The vocabulary document is hidden during the quiz so you "
"cannot cheat. Maybe you want to start with a flashcard session, then you can "
"move on to a multiple choice quiz or do the powerful question and answer "
"quiz. You get instant feedback on correct and incorrect answers and you have "
"the option to repeat any errors, further improving your learning efficiency. "
"If you need a little extra help you can use the hint function."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "Vocabulary documents"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kwordquiz; can open several types of vocabulary data. Supported are .kvtml "
"used by other &kde; programs such as &kvoctrain;, .wql used by WordQuiz for "
"&Windows;, .csv files with comma-separated text, and .xml.gz files created "
"by Pauker (http://pauker.sourceforge.net). You can automatically combine "
"several documents to one large list if you need to practice for &eg; a final "
"exam."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kwordquiz; can save your vocabulary documents several different formats. "
"The default is the .kvtml format used by other &kde; programs. Other "
"available options are the .wql format used by WordQuiz for &Windows; "
"allowing exchange with &Windows; users, .csv, and .html."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can have several files open at the same time and easily copy or move "
"entries between files."
msgstr ""

